Spec: Area filter

Purpose:
  Whether a ride's outline comes within a radius of a pinned point; the "rides around here" filter.

Owns:
  ./area_filter.dart
  /test/domain/area_filter_test.dart

References:
  /docs/decisions/0001-ride-outlines.md
  /lib/domain/ride_outline.sdd
  /lib/features/history_map/history_map.sdd

Must:
  @AreaFilter holds a pin (latitude, longitude) and a radius in km from `1` to `50` in steps of `1`;
    a radius outside that range is clamped and then rounded to a whole kilometre. The default radius is `5` km.
  @AreaFilter.matches is true when any segment of the outline passes within the radius of the pin, so a ride
    that only touches the circle counts; the distance is that of the nearest segment.
  The outline's bounds, grown by the radius, reject far rides before any segment is measured.
  The bounds test also accepts a pin across `±180` from the outline (the pin longitude a whole turn east or
    west), so a ride beside the antimeridian matches from either side (#100).
  An outline with fewer than two points never matches.
  Distances are metres on the sphere used by the shared @DistanceCalculator and stay within `1` % of it for
    radii up to `50` km.

Must not:
  Read trackpoints, the database, the map package or the clock.

Scenario: ride crosses the circle
  Given a pin and a radius of `5` km
  When an outline passes `3` km from the pin
  Then it matches

Scenario: ride stays outside
  Given a pin and a radius of `5` km
  When every point of an outline is more than `5` km away but a segment passes `8` km from the pin
  Then it does not match

Example:
  radius `0` or below: clamped to `1`
  radius `80`: clamped to `50`
  radius `7.4`: rounded to `7`; radius `0.4`: clamped to `1`
  an outline that ends exactly `5` km from the pin at radius `5`: matches
